Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: count depth/stencil samples once in GMEM layout

The resource layout's cpp already includes its sample count. Multiplying
it by the framebuffer sample count again overestimates depth/stencil GMEM
storage: a four-byte Z24S8 attachment at 4x MSAA is accounted as 64 bytes
per pixel instead of 16.

On the Fairphone 3's Adreno 506 (136 KiB GMEM), the reported 64x32 batch
with color cpp=4 and Z/S cpp=64 needs 144 KiB after 16 KiB alignment. Even
the minimum tile cannot fit, so calc_nbins() keeps searching until integer
overflow. Correct Z/S accounting reduces that layout to 48 KiB.

Compute bytes per sample from each plane's layout format, then multiply
by framebuffer samples once, as the color-buffer path already does. Use
the separate stencil plane's own format, and retain the framebuffer sample
count rather than assuming it always equals the resource sample count.

This fixes the inflated accounting, not the separate need to bound the
tile search for genuinely impossible layouts.

Target: Mesa 26.1.8
Link: https://github.com/emerge-elixir/emerge/issues/82
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -462,9 +462,15 @@
 
    if (has_zs || assume_zs) {
       struct fd_resource *rsc = fd_resource(pfb->zsbuf.texture);
-      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+      /* layout.cpp already includes the resource's sample count.  Start
+       * from each plane's format so framebuffer samples are counted once,
+       * just as for color buffers below.
+       */
+      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] =
+         util_format_get_blocksize(rsc->layout.format) * pfb->samples;
       if (rsc->stencil)
-         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] =
+            util_format_get_blocksize(rsc->stencil->layout.format) * pfb->samples;
 
       /* If we clear z or s but not both, and we are using z24s8 (ie.
        * !separate_stencil) then we need to restore the other, even if
